    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="1055" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1039"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/5–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Legation in Switzerland
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-20T13:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Unpal 110. For Lausanne. We agree (Palun 153<anchor n="1" xml:id="d677-f1"/>) ur
                    proposal France and Turkey join US and UK in concerted program urge Israel and
                    Arabs face refugee problem constructively through repatriation and resettlement.
                    Pls outline to Yalcin and Boisanger genl nature our approaches Israel and Arabs
                    (Depcirtel Apr 29, 5 p. m. and Unpal 85, Apr 28), informing them Dept concurs
                    your view re desirability parallel approaches by French and Turkish Govts and
                    requesting that they so inform their Govts earliest opportunity. In absence
                    instrs this subject to French and Turk missions Washington, we believe approach
                    by you speedier and more effective.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
